    "body": "### Motivation\n- Implement the `POST /api/users/register` endpoint to allow new users to sign up with email and password.\n- Enforce acceptance criteria: validate email format, require password length >= 8, enforce unique email, and return proper HTTP status codes.\n- Apply business rules to block temporary email domains (e.g., `tempmail.com`) and prevent passwords containing the email prefix.\n\n### Description\n- Added a Spring Boot application scaffold (`Viom16Application`) and project configuration (`pom.xml`) targeting Java 21 and Spring Boot.\n- Implemented controller `UserRegistrationController`, service `UserRegistrationService`, models (`User`, `UserRegistrationRequest`, `UserRegistrationResponse`), exception classes, and an `ApiExceptionHandler` for mapping errors to `400`/`409` responses.\n- Added an `InMemoryUserRepository` implementing `UserRepository` for simple persistence and added SHA-256 password hashing in the service.\n- Added integration tests `UserRegistrationControllerTest` covering successful registration, validation failures, business-rule failures, and duplicate-email handling, and a CI workflow `.github/workflows/ci.yml` that runs `mvn -B test`.\n\n### Testing\n- Ran `mvn -B test` in the workspace, which attempted to run the added tests but failed due to Maven dependency resolution being blocked with a `403` from `repo.maven.apache.org` (tests could not complete).\n- The test suite was added and designed to assert the acceptance criteria via `MockMvc`, but results could not be validated end-to-end because of the dependency download failure.\n\n------\n[Codex Task](https://chatgpt.com/codex/tasks/task_e_697729cc0af88325a32478bc0010e1dc)",
